     1	# Re-sending the saved requests behind the two untraced misses: protocol
     2	
     3	2026-11-11. Written before any send; revised after the council's challenge (`council/b-codex.md`) and after a finding at no cost
     4	(below). Part of the round in [LOG.md](LOG.md). Nothing in any step, prompt, rule or saved run changes.
     5	
     6	## Found at no cost before the send (`refusal_census.py`)
     7	
     8	Draw 3's judge first answered the China share question on 2026-07-08 with **rung 4**, the rung draws 1 and 2 chose that day. The
     9	frozen check refused that answer because it named the export-controls theme (v8) as a dependency ("v8 is not a dependency of v17");
    10	the day then re-asked with a note, and the re-sent answer was **rung 5**, which the question kept to the window end. Over the six
    11	draws, 65 judgements were refused and re-asked (clean 10, 16, 18; production 10, 5, 6); 42 of the refusals are this one, on this
    12	question. The re-sent answer changed the rung 8 times; 4 of the 8 are on the China share question (clean draw 2 on 07-05, clean
    13	draw 3 on 07-08, production draw 1 on 07-08 and 07-12, production draw 4 on 07-02); clean draw 3's and production draw 4's changes
    14	held to the window end and both are misses on the ruler.
    15	
    16	## What the sends decide
    17	
    18	- China share: whether, on draw 3's first request of 07-08, rung 4 is the judge's usual answer (then the refusal and its re-ask turned
    19	  an agreeing answer into the miss) or a minority one (then the re-ask only drew the usual answer); and whether the note added on the
    20	  re-ask itself moves the rung.
    21	- FY2028 revenue: whether draw 2's window-end request and draw 3's differ in what the judge answers, or each allows both answers.
    22	
    23	## The cases (`resend.py`; requests rebuilt by the offline replay of each draw)
    24	
    25	| Case | Request | Saved answer to it |
    26	|---|---|---|
    27	| A. draw 3, China share, 07-08, first | the day's first request, whose answer the check refused | rung 4, refused (theme named as a dependency) |
    28	| F. draw 3, China share, 07-08, accepted | the same request with the re-ask note | rung 5, kept |
    29	| B. draw 1, China share, 07-08, accepted | the request of a draw that moved to rung 4 that day | rung 4, kept |
    30	| C. draw 3, China share, 07-14, accepted | the window end of the miss | rung 5, kept |
    31	| D. draw 2, FY2028 revenue, 07-14, accepted | the window end of the miss (one "41%" item, 19 items, previous rung 3) | rung 3, kept |
    32	| E. draw 3, FY2028 revenue, 07-14, accepted | the window end of a draw that agrees (two "41%" items, 24 items, previous rung 3) | rung 2, kept |
    33	
    34	Three sends a case, 18 in all, interleaved and sent at once through the production transport, no archive, one spending limit.
    35	Cost: about $0.04 expected; $0.65 if every send were tried three times at its worst; cap $0.70.
    36	
    37	`resend.py check` passed for all six, with no send: each request equals, sorted, the saved archive's request and, as production
    38	serializes it, what `model.build_request` builds today; each draw's ledger is rebuilt and stopped before that day's judging round; on
    39	it the saved kept answers pass the frozen check, case A's saved answer is refused again for the same reason, and an answer citing an
    40	id the request does not show is refused.
    41	
    42	## Reading rule, fixed now
    43	
    44	Each answer is read for its rung, and for whether the frozen check accepts it. **An answer the check refuses still counts for its
    45	rung**, since every refusal seen here is about which ids are cited; refusals are reported beside, with their reason. A case with
    46	fewer than three answers that carry a rung decides nothing.
    47	
    48	- **A.** Rung 4 in at least two of three: on that request rung 4 is the judge's usual answer, and the refusal with its re-ask turned it
    49	  into the miss (supports the refusal as the cause). Rung 5 in at least two of three: the re-ask only drew the usual answer (the refusal
    50	  is not shown to be the cause). Anything else: not decided.
    51	- **F against A.** If F's rungs sit lower (toward 5) than A's by two or more answers, the note itself may move the rung; otherwise the
    52	  note is not shown to matter.
    53	- **B.** Read beside A: if both give mostly 4, draw 3's and draw 1's inputs of that day are not shown to differ in what they produce.
    54	- **C.** Rung 5 in three of three: the window-end request holds the rung the question reached. A rung 4 in any: the window-end answer is
    55	  itself open. Neither says why the saved run chose 5.
    56	- **D, E.** D at rung 3 in three of three and E at rung 2 in three of three: the requests differ in what they produce, a lead to trace
    57	  (not which difference matters). Both mixed: each request allows both answers. Any other pattern: not decided. In D, whether any
    58	  answer again reads $553 billion as below the $550 billion floor.
    59	
    60	## What it cannot say
    61	
    62	Three answers a case give no rate. Nothing here covers other days or other questions. An outcome that supports the refusal as the
    63	cause of the China miss still leaves the window-end rung as the product of every later day.
     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Re-send saved judge requests of the D392 clean draws as production sends them, several times each, and read the answers through the
     3	frozen judge's own checks. Each send is a fresh answer: no archive stands in between.
     4	
     5	A case is (draw, question, day, which): `accepted` is the request whose answer the saved run accepted for that question on that day;
     6	`first` is the day's first request of that question when the check refused its answer and the day re-asked with a note. Both come
     7	from the offline replay of the draw (`poc/data/clean-e2e-misses-2026-11-11/control-d<N>/control-requests.json`, which reproduced every saved
     8	request of the draw). The answers are checked against the draw's ledger as it stood before that day's judging round, rebuilt by the
     9	same replay stopped there.
    10	
    11	  resend.py check --case 3 v17 2026-07-08 first [--case ...]         no send: every identity below, the ledgers, the worst cost
    12	  resend.py send  <new folder> --case ... [--sends 3]                 the sends, all cases interleaved and concurrent, one spending limit
    13	  resend.py read  <send folder> --case ...                            each answer through the schema and the frozen check; rungs by case
    14	
    15	Checks before any send, each refusing the run: the request's sorted form is the saved archive's request of the accepted answer, byte
    16	for byte; the request as production serializes it (json.dumps in the order model.build_request builds) equals what build_request
    17	builds today from its system and user text; the saved accepted answer passes the frozen check against the rebuilt ledger (positive
    18	control; for a `first` case, the saved refused answer is refused again), and the same answer with a citation of an id the request
    19	does not show is refused (negative control). An answer the check refuses still has its rung read: the refusal is about citations."""
    20	import argparse, concurrent.futures, contextlib, glob, hashlib, json, sqlite3, sys, threading, time
    21	from pathlib import Path
    22	
    23	HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
    24	ROOT = HERE.parents[1]
    25	sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
    26	sys.path[:0] = [str(ROOT / 'clean-arch/step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10')]
    27	import edge_replay  # noqa: E402  (puts clean-arch/e2e-2026-11-09 and src on the path)
    28	import budget  # noqa: E402
    29	from hivemind import config, model  # noqa: E402
    30	from hivemind.views import judging  # noqa: E402
    31	
    32	DATA = ROOT / 'poc/data/clean-e2e-misses-2026-11-11'
    33	CAP_USD = 0.70
    34	
    35	
    36	class StopBeforeRound(Exception):
    37	    pass
    38	
    39	
    40	def sha256(text):
    41	    return hashlib.sha256(text.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()
    42	
    43	
    44	def saved_first_request(draw, view, day):
    45	    """The day's first request of the question, when its answer was refused: the refused row of the saved archive, and the reason the
    46	    check gives for it."""
    47	    edge_replay.use_draw(draw)
    48	    rounds = json.loads((DATA / f'control-d{draw}' / 'control-rounds.json').read_text())
    49	    entries = [entry for entry in rounds.get(day, []) if entry['view'] == view]
    50	    if len(entries) < 2:
    51	        raise SystemExit(f'draw {draw} asked {view} once on {day}: there is no refused first request')
    52	    first_sha = entries[0]['sha256']
    53	    with contextlib.closing(sqlite3.connect(f"file:{edge_replay.SAVED / 'archive.sqlite'}?mode=ro", uri=True)) as conn:
    54	        rows = conn.execute("select request_sha256, request_json, answer_json from model_calls where request_sha256 like ?", (first_sha + ':refused:%',)).fetchall()
    55	    if len(rows) != 1:
    56	        raise SystemExit(f'draw {draw} {view} {day}: {len(rows)} refused rows for the first request')
    57	    _, request_json, answer_json = rows[0]
    58	    with contextlib.closing(sqlite3.connect(f"file:{edge_replay.SAVED / 'views.sqlite'}?mode=ro", uri=True)) as conn:
    59	        rung = conn.execute('select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day=?', (view, day)).fetchone()[0]
    60	    return {'request_sha256': first_sha, 'rung': rung, 'request_json': request_json, 'answer': json.loads(answer_json)}
    61	
    62	
    63	def saved_judgement(draw, view, day):
    64	    edge_replay.use_draw(draw)
    65	    with contextlib.closing(sqlite3.connect(f"file:{edge_replay.SAVED / 'views.sqlite'}?mode=ro", uri=True)) as conn:
    66	        row = conn.execute('select request_sha256, rung, seq from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day=?', (view, day)).fetchone()
    67	    if not row:
    68	        raise SystemExit(f'draw {draw} has no judgement of {view} on {day}')
    69	    request_sha, rung, seq = row
    70	    with contextlib.closing(sqlite3.connect(f"file:{edge_replay.SAVED / 'archive.sqlite'}?mode=ro", uri=True)) as conn:
    71	        request_json, answer_json = conn.execute('select request_json, answer_json from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (request_sha,)).fetchone()
    72	    return {'request_sha256': request_sha, 'rung': rung, 'seq': seq, 'request_json': request_json, 'answer': json.loads(answer_json)}
    73	
    74	
    75	def ledger_before(draw, day):
    76	    """The draw's ledger after the articles of `day` and before its judging round, rebuilt once by the offline replay."""
    77	    folder = DATA / f'ledger-d{draw}-before-{day}'
    78	    if (folder / 'views.sqlite').exists() and (folder / 'stopped-before.json').exists():
    79	        return folder / 'views.sqlite'
    80	    edge_replay.use_draw(draw)
    81	    production_judge = edge_replay.e2e_adapter.Adapter.judge
    82	
    83	    def stop_or_judge(self, round_day, seq, changed):
    84	        if round_day == day:
    85	            raise StopBeforeRound(round_day)
    86	        return production_judge(self, round_day, seq, changed)
    87	
    88	    edge_replay.e2e_adapter.Adapter.judge = stop_or_judge
    89	    try:
    90	        edge_replay.run_replay(folder, edge_replay.STEP2)
    91	        raise SystemExit(f'the replay of draw {draw} never reached a judging round on {day}')
    92	    except StopBeforeRound:
    93	        pass
    94	    finally:
    95	        edge_replay.e2e_adapter.Adapter.judge = production_judge
    96	    (folder / 'stopped-before.json').write_text(json.dumps({'draw': draw, 'day': day, 'saved run': str(edge_replay.SAVED)}))
    97	    return folder / 'views.sqlite'
    98	
    99	
   100	def read_only(path):
   101	    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{Path(path).resolve()}?mode=ro', uri=True)
   102	    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row
   103	    return conn
   104	
   105	
   106	def load_case(draw, view, day, which='accepted'):
   107	    if which not in ('accepted', 'first'):
   108	        raise SystemExit(f'a case is the accepted or the first request, not {which}')
   109	    saved = saved_judgement(draw, view, day) if which == 'accepted' else saved_first_request(draw, view, day)
   110	    requests = json.loads((DATA / f'control-d{draw}' / 'control-requests.json').read_text())
   111	    report = json.loads((DATA / f'control-d{draw}' / 'control-report.json').read_text())
   112	    if not report['passed'] or report['saved run'] != str(edge_replay.SAVED):
   113	        raise SystemExit(f'the offline replay of draw {draw} did not pass or is of another run')
   114	    request = requests.get(saved['request_sha256'])
   115	    if request is None:
   116	        raise SystemExit(f'the replay of draw {draw} holds no request {saved["request_sha256"]}')
   117	    canonical = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)
   118	    if canonical != saved['request_json'] or sha256(canonical) != saved['request_sha256']:
   119	        raise SystemExit(f'draw {draw} {view} {day}: the rebuilt request is not the saved one')
   120	    cfg = config.load(edge_replay.e2e_adapter.CONFIG)
   121	    rebuilt = model.build_request(cfg.rejudging, request['messages'][0]['content'], request['messages'][-1]['content'],
   122	                                  judging.schema_for(cfg.rejudging.prompt_version), 'judgement', cfg.provider)
   123	    if json.dumps(rebuilt) != json.dumps(request):
   124	        raise SystemExit(f'draw {draw} {view} {day}: the request is not, byte for byte, what model.build_request builds today')
   125	    ledger = ledger_before(draw, day)
   126	    with contextlib.closing(read_only(ledger)) as conn:
   127	        if conn.execute('select 1 from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day=?', (view, day)).fetchone():
   128	            raise SystemExit(f'the ledger before {day} already holds that day\'s judgement of {view}')
   129	        user = request['messages'][-1]['content']
   130	        errors = judging.check_answer(conn, view, saved['answer'], user)
   131	        refused = judging.check_answer(conn, view, {**saved['answer'], 'cites': saved['answer']['cites'] + ['e999999']}, user)
   132	    if which == 'accepted' and errors:
   133	        raise SystemExit(f'draw {draw} {view} {day}: the saved answer fails the check on the rebuilt ledger: {errors}')
   134	    if which == 'first' and not errors:
   135	        raise SystemExit(f'draw {draw} {view} {day}: the saved refused answer passes the check on the rebuilt ledger')
   136	    if not refused:
   137	        raise SystemExit(f'draw {draw} {view} {day}: negative control failed, an unshown citation was not refused')
   138	    return {'key': f'd{draw}-{view}-{day}-{which}', 'draw': draw, 'view': view, 'day': day, 'which': which, 'request': request,
   139	            'ledger': str(ledger), 'saved rung': saved['rung'], 'saved answer': saved['answer'], 'saved answer rung': saved['answer']['rung'],
   140	            'saved answer refused for': errors, 'as sent sha256': sha256(json.dumps(request)), 'worst cost per attempt (usd)': budget.worst_cost(request)}
   141	
   142	
   143	def cases_of(arguments):
   144	    return [load_case(int(draw), view, day, which) for draw, view, day, which in arguments.case]
   145	
   146	
   147	def facts(cases, sends):
   148	    worst = sum(case['worst cost per attempt (usd)'] for case in cases) * sends * budget.ATTEMPTS
   149	    return {'cases': {case['key']: {'saved rung': case['saved rung'], 'saved answer to this request': case['saved answer rung'],
   150	                                    'saved answer refused for': case['saved answer refused for'], 'as sent sha256': case['as sent sha256'], 'ledger': case['ledger'],
   151	                                    'user text characters': len(case['request']['messages'][-1]['content'])} for case in cases},
   152	            'sends per case': sends, 'sends': sends * len(cases), 'worst cost, every send tried three times (usd)': round(worst, 4), 'cap (usd)': CAP_USD}
   153	
   154	
   155	def send(cases, output, sends):
   156	    registered = facts(cases, sends)
   157	    if registered['worst cost, every send tried three times (usd)'] > CAP_USD:
   158	        raise SystemExit('the worst cost passes the cap')
   159	    output = Path(output).resolve()
   160	    if DATA.resolve() not in output.parents:
   161	        raise SystemExit(f'the sends are written only under {DATA}')
   162	    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)
   163	    (output / 'raw').mkdir()
   164	    (output / 'registration.json').write_text(json.dumps({**registered, 'registered at': time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z')}, indent=1))
   165	    current = threading.local()
   166	
   167	    def attempt(provider, request):
   168	        """One attempt through the production transport; the body is on disk before anything else reads it."""
   169	        current.attempts += 1
   170	        response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)
   171	        (output / 'raw' / f'{current.name}-attempt-{current.attempts}.json').write_text(json.dumps(response, ensure_ascii=False))
   172	        current.returned = response
   173	        return response
   174	
   175	    limit = budget.Budget(CAP_USD, attempt=attempt)
   176	    provider = config.load(edge_replay.e2e_adapter.CONFIG).provider
   177	
   178	    def one(job):
   179	        case, number = job
